lower is better)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.6 &#x000b1; 2.6</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4.5 &#x000b1; 2.1</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.7 &#x000b1; 2.3</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Fatigue (last two weeks) (scale 0&#x02013;10, lower is better)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.1 &#x000b1; 2.8</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.0 &#x000b1; 2.7</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.4 &#x000b1; 2.8</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Six Minute Walk Test (ft)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1050.0 &#x000b1; 434.3</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1059.8 &#x000b1; 348.7</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1103.6 &#x000b1; 267.3</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Squat Test (depth in cm)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">36.3 &#x000b1; 17.2</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">10.0 &#x000b1; 12.4</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">42.3 &#x000b1; 28.2</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Timed Functional Walking Test (seconds)</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.7 &#x000b1; 7.2</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">18.7 &#x000b1; 5.4</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">17.5 &#x000b1; 5.1</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Number of subjects at Test-1</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">102</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">37</td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">54</td></tr><tr><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Number of subjects at Test-6w</td><td valign="top"